  "notes": "Columbia, Santa Maria pressing denoted by \"S\" etch in runouts.\nTan/brown steamboat Reprise labels with no Warners logo or address in the perimeter text.\n\nRecord 1 - Sides A & D\nRecord 2 - Sides B & C\n\nBack of sleeve states \"Produced by Ray Davies and Shel Talmy\"; labels state \"Produced by Ray Davies\"\n\nA1, A6, B3, C4, D1. Hill & Range Songs, Inc. BMI\nA2, A3, A7, B1, B4, B5, B7, C2, C5, C7, D3, D6, D7. Noma Music, Inc. / Hi-Count Music, Inc. BMI\nA4, B6, C1, D5. Noma Music, Inc.\nA5, C6. (From the Soundtrack of the film \"Percy\") Al Gallico Music Corp. BMI\nB2, D4. Abkco Music, Inc. / Noma Music, Inc. BMI\nC3. Warner-Tamerlane Pub. Corp. BMI\nD2. Noma Music, Inc. / Abkco Music, Inc. BMI\n\nReprise Records, a Division of Warner Bros. Records Inc.\nMade in U.S.A.\nPrinted in U.S.A.\n\nSome copies issued with \"Promotional Copy Not For Sale\" stickers on cover.\n\nAlthough labels indicate Stereo on all sides, some tracks were never released in Stereo. Mono tracks not indicated on this release.\n\nRunouts are etched. ",
  "released_formatted": "Mar 1972",
